# {{ component.name }}

A minimal React + TypeScript browser scaffold. `src/app/App.tsx` displays the project name and scaffold status.
There are no business features, API integrations or global state. This is a Vite client, not Next.js/RSC/server actions.

## Code and responsibilities

- `index.html`, `src/app/main.tsx`: document and React mount entrypoints.
- `src/app/App.tsx`: the static screen; `app/` owns composition, not a framework router.
- `src/features/`: real features; `src/shared/components/` and `src/shared/lib/`: demonstrated reusable code.
- `tests/`: guidance for future cross-feature checks; no product unit/E2E tests exist yet.

Define component props, user behavior and incoming API contracts. Keep local UI state near its owner; do not duplicate
server-side business authority. Effects must own cancellation and stale-result guards for requests, subscriptions and
timers. Do not disguise loading, empty or error states as success. The current scaffold has no external I/O or resources.

## Environment and checks

Use Node 22.12 or later and npm 11.11.0. Separate installation/lock creation from checks and builds.

```sh
npm install
npm run check
```

Keep the generated `package-lock.json`; use `npm ci` for later reproducible installs. This component owns its npm
environment and lock. `check` runs strict typechecking and a Vite production build, not browser, accessibility or product
tests. `npm run dev` starts a separate development server; do not run it merely to verify prose.
Client-exposed environment values are not secret storage.

These pins were checked against npm registry metadata on 2026-10-26. Review peers, Node compatibility and the lock together
when changing versions:

- [React 19.3.1](https://registry.npmjs.org/react/19.3.1), [react-dom 19.3.1](https://registry.npmjs.org/react-dom/19.3.1)
- [Vite 8.3.5](https://registry.npmjs.org/vite/8.3.5), [TypeScript 7.0.2](https://registry.npmjs.org/typescript/7.0.2)
- [@types/react 19.3.0](https://registry.npmjs.org/@types%2Freact/19.3.0),
